      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "summary": "What this topic covers.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "topic-map",
          "html": "<p>Your browser is the window you use to see almost everything online &mdash; and the window works both ways. Websites, advertisers and trackers can read a lot about you through it: what you visit, what you click, and enough details about your device to recognise you again later. Choosing a private browser and setting it up well removes most of that tracking without changing how you use the web.</p>"
        }
      ]
